## Sources

Make/model/generation/engine facts were compiled, collapsed, and normalized
from publicly available information on autoevolution.com. Egypt-market
additions (e.g. Speranza, El Nasr) are original curation by this project.

A further set of brands that autoevolution.com does not cover (see
`data/open-data-sources.json` for the per-brand list) was compiled from open
data, with years derived from vehicle registrations and therefore approximate:

- RDW open data (Dutch vehicle registry, "Gekentekende voertuigen") — public
  domain / CC0, attribution: Team Open Data RDW.
- European Environment Agency / European Commission DG CLIMA, "Monitoring of
  CO2 emissions from passenger cars" — CC BY 4.0. Contains data from the
  European Environment Agency.
- Wikidata — CC0 (model names and, where present, production dates).
- U.S. EPA / DOE fueleconomy.gov — U.S. government public domain (Geo).

